"{\n  \"agreementDate\": \"15th November, 2022\",\n  \"placeOfSigning\": \"Ahmedabad\",\n  \"parties\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"SABARMATI CAPITAL TWO LIMITED\",\n      \"address\": \"Office No. 2, 28th Floor, GIFT One Building, Road – 5C, Zone 5, GIFT City, Gandhinagar - 382355\",\n      \"phone\": \"079 6674 1150\",\n      \"email\": \"Yashwantsingh.chauhan@ilfsindia.com\",\n      \"CIN\": \"\",\n      \"PAN\": \"\",\n      \"GST\": \"\",\n      \"obligations\": [\n        {\n          \"clauseNumber\": \"3.1\",\n          \"description\": \"Provision of Services\",\n          \"clauseText\": \"AGENCY shall provide the Services to SCTL for the Term, unless determined in accordance with Clause 6 hereof. AGENCY shall provide the Services in a timely, efficient and orderly manner, in accordance with Annexure I hereto and as per the General Terms and Conditions more particularly mentioned in Clause 9 hereof. AGENCY shall ensure that all statutory provisions and requirements (including but not limited to all payments, emoluments etc. labour laws, safety standards and other applicable acts for its scope of work) in respect of the Services to be rendered under this Agreement or the conduct of AGENCY employees while on or in the Premises shall be complied with by Agency. It is clarified that the employees of AGENCY shall, for all purposes and to all intents, be the employees of AGENCY and all compliance liabilities on account of such employees, will be that of AGENCY and SCTL in no manner be liable for the same.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"clauseNumber\": \"3.2\",\n          \"description\": \"Confidentiality\",\n          \"clauseText\": \"Agency and its employees, retainers, consultants, its sub – contractors, employees/staff of the sub- contractor(s) engaged by AGENCY, shall not divulge or allow to be divulged, during Term of this Agreement and for a period of TWO years after expiry of Term efflux of time or early termination of this Agreement (as the case may be) to any person any confidential information relating to the business or affairs of SCTL or the Premises covered by this Agreement to which AGENCY, its employees, retainers, consultants, its sub – contractors, employees/staff of the sub-contractor(s) engaged by Agency may have access in the course of rendering the Services, except to the extent necessary for performance of the Services.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"clauseNumber\": \"3.4(a)\",\n          \"description\": \"Indemnity\",\n          \"clauseText\": \"AGENCY hereby agrees to indemnify and keep indemnified SCTL, directors and employees from and against any and all loss, damage or liability (whether civil or criminal) incurred, suffered (including reasonable legal fees and costs incurred by SCTL) directly or indirectly resulting from or relating to the following: (i) Any act of gross negligence or wilful misconduct of its employees or agents or sub-contractors; (ii) Breaches in respect of any confidentiality obligations in rendering of the Services pursuant to this Agreement (ii) Any non-compliance of applicable laws by AGENCY and its employees, retainers, consultants, its sub-contractors, employees/staff of the sub-contractor(s) engaged by Agency. This indemnity however is subject to mutual determination that the loss is attributable to a breach on the part of AGENCY, its employees, or its agents and Agency shall present all the data and evidence required for such determination.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"clauseNumber\": \"3.5\",\n          \"description\": \"Labour Law Compliance\",\n          \"clauseText\": \"AGENCY shall employ competent, experienced staff / employees / personnel for the purpose of providing the Services. This Agreement does not and shall not be construed to create any employer-employee or principal–agent relationship between SCTL and any employees, contract labour, representatives and personnel engaged by AGENCY in the performance of Services. AGENCY, inter alia, agrees that the Services shall be rendered in strict compliance with the provisions of all applicable laws. AGENCY shall make statutory payments/remittances, applicable tax deductions etc. as are required to be made under labour related and other applicable laws. SCTL reserves the right to recover from AGENCY or withhold any amounts payable to AGENCY towards discharge of any statutory obligations arising out of the breach of any of the contract labour laws or other applicable laws by AGENCY, without prejudice to any of its rights and other remedies herein stated or available under other applicable laws.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Quess Corp Limited\",\n      \"address\": \"3/3/2, Bellandur Gate, Sarjapur Road, Bangalore – 560103\",\n      \"phone\": \"7507411554\",\n      \"email\": \"samarth.awasthi@quesscorp.com\",\n      \"CIN\": \"L74140KA2007PLC043909\",\n      \"PAN\": \"\",\n      \"GST\": \"\",\n      \"obligations\": [\n        {\n          \"clauseNumber\": \"3.1\",\n          \"description\": \"Provision of Services\",\n          \"clauseText\": \"AGENCY shall provide the Services to SCTL for the Term, unless determined in accordance with Clause 6 hereof. AGENCY shall provide the Services in a timely, efficient and orderly manner, in accordance with Annexure I hereto and as per the General Terms and Conditions more particularly mentioned in Clause 9 hereof. AGENCY shall ensure that all statutory provisions and requirements (including but not limited to all payments, emoluments etc. labour laws, safety standards and other applicable acts for its scope of work) in respect of the Services to be rendered under this Agreement or the conduct of AGENCY employees while on or in the Premises shall be complied with by Agency. It is clarified that the employees of AGENCY shall, for all purposes and to all intents, be the employees of AGENCY and all compliance liabilities on account of such employees, will be that of AGENCY and SCTL in no manner be liable for the same.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"clauseNumber\": \"3.2\",\n          \"description\": \"Confidentiality\",\n          \"clauseText\": \"Agency and its employees, retainers, consultants, its sub – contractors, employees/staff of the sub- contractor(s) engaged by AGENCY, shall not divulge or allow to be divulged, during Term of this Agreement and for a period of TWO years after expiry of Term efflux of time or early termination of this Agreement (as the case may be) to any person any confidential information relating to the business or affairs of SCTL or the Premises covered by this Agreement to which AGENCY, its employees, retainers, consultants, its sub – contractors, employees/staff of the sub-contractor(s) engaged by Agency may have access in the course of rendering the Services, except to the extent necessary for performance of the Services.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"clauseNumber\": \"3.3\",\n          \"description\": \"Delegation/ Sub-contracting\",\n          \"clauseText\": \"AGENCY shall be allowed to delegate or sub-contract any of its duties or obligations arising under this Agreement with prior approval from SCTL in writing, however AGENCY shall be entirely responsible for the overall Services and liable for duties, activities and obligations undertaken by the sub-contractor.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"clauseNumber\": \"3.4(a)\",\n          \"description\": \"Indemnity\",\n          \"clauseText\": \"AGENCY hereby agrees to indemnify and keep indemnified SCTL, directors and employees from and against any and all loss, damage or liability (whether civil or criminal) incurred, suffered (including reasonable legal fees and costs incurred by SCTL) directly or indirectly resulting from or relating to the following: (i) Any act of gross negligence or wilful misconduct of its employees or agents or sub-contractors; (ii) Breaches in respect of any confidentiality obligations in rendering of the Services pursuant to this Agreement (ii) Any non-compliance of applicable laws by AGENCY and its employees, retainers, consultants, its sub-contractors, employees/staff of the sub-contractor(s) engaged by Agency. This indemnity however is subject to mutual determination that the loss is attributable to a breach on the part of AGENCY, its employees, or its agents and Agency shall present all the data and evidence required for such determination.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"clauseNumber\": \"3.5\",\n          \"description\": \"Labour Law Compliance\",\n          \"clauseText\": \"AGENCY shall employ competent, experienced staff / employees / personnel for the purpose of providing the Services. This Agreement does not and shall not be construed to create any employer-employee or principal–agent relationship between SCTL and any employees, contract labour, representatives and personnel engaged by AGENCY in the performance of Services. AGENCY, inter alia, agrees that the Services shall be rendered in strict compliance with the provisions of all applicable laws. AGENCY shall make statutory payments/remittances, applicable tax deductions etc. as are required to be made under labour related and other applicable laws. SCTL reserves the right to recover from AGENCY or withhold any amounts payable to AGENCY towards discharge of any statutory obligations arising out of the breach of any of the contract labour laws or other applicable laws by AGENCY, without prejudice to any of its rights and other remedies herein stated or available under other applicable laws.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"penalty_clauses\": [\n    {\n      \"clauseNumber\": \"9\",\n      \"description\": \"Liquidated Damages\",\n      \"penaltyDetails\": \"In the event of AGENCY failing to comply with the agreed service levels (SLAs), SCTL at its discretion shall make AGENCY liable to pay liquidated damages at 1% of Management Fee per week of delay subject to a maximum of 10% of Management fee, shall be deducted as Liquidated Damages. The Parties agree that these liquidity damages are the genuine pre-estimate of the damages that are likely to be caused to the SCTL and are not levied by way of a penalty.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"clauseNumber\": \"5.34\",\n      \"description\": \"Shortfall in Daily Manpower\",\n      \"penaltyDetails\": \"Any shortfall in daily manpower deputed at site without any reliever penalty will be charged at Rs. 1000/- (Rupees One Thousand) per day per employee along with employee daily wages, if employees is on leave / absent for more than 3 days.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"arbitration_clause\": {\n    \"amicable_settlement\": \"All disputes, controversies or differences which may arise between the Parties out of or in relation to or in connection with this Agreement, including any issue as to this Agreement’s validity or enforceability, or for the construction, termination or breach thereof, shall be decided amicably by the Parties.\",\n    \"arbitration\": \"If such dispute, controversy or difference cannot be amicably settled by the Parties within 21 (twenty one) calendar days after written notice by one Party to the other Party (the “Arbitration Notice”), the matter shall be finally settled by arbitration conducted in accordance with the provisions of the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996 by a sole arbitrator appointed by SCTL.\",\n    \"arbitral_tribunal\": \"Sole arbitrator appointed by SCTL.\",\n    \"final_and_binding\": \"The costs of arbitration shall be borne in accordance with the determination by the Arbitrators. Except in the case of termination, the Parties shall continue to perform all their obligations under this Agreement pending the arbitration award.\",\n    \"seat_and_venue\": \"The venue of such arbitration shall be Mumbai.\",\n    \"language\": \"The language of arbitration proceedings shall be English.\"\n  }\n}"